{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791623360072,"sessionID":"ses_edaed43d5ffeRlWR2XlMWa9yDH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_fAxrBBaiHo67HcuAtJ7u9107","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Assessment: funnel icon usage\n2: \n3: id: drama\n4: status: open\n5: date: 2026-08-16\n6: \n7: ## Summary\n8: \n9: The `funnel` icon (`@lucide/svelte/icons/funnel`) is used in **7 places** across the codebase. Exactly **one** of them is a semantically correct use of a funnel — the library filter button in `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte`. The remaining **6** are all mobile navigation/drawer toggles, where the funnel icon is inappropriate: users reading a funnel expect \"filter this list\", but the button actually opens a navigation drawer/menu. This assessment recommends replacing every non-filter usage with a `menu` (hamburger) icon, which the codebase already ships as `HamburgerButton` (used by settings).\n10: \n11: ## 1. Where the funnel icon is used (full audit)\n12: \n13: ### 1.1 Direct `IconFunnel` renders (visible funnel icons)\n14: \n15: | # | File | Line(s) | Context | Kind |\n16: |---|------|---------|---------|------|\n17: | 1 | `src/lib/components/ui/buttons/FunnelButton.svelte` | 2, 15 | Floating circular button (`absolute`, `lg:hidden` = mobile-only), renders `<IconFunnel class=\"text-c-neutral-1\" />`. This is the icon *source* for every `FunnelButton` consumer. | Icon source for mobile toggles |\n18: | 2 | `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte` | 2, 60 | `<IconFunnel />` inside the libraries filter button; clicking opens the filter dropdown (genres, rating, wishlist, lent books, recipe/plant filters, clear filters). | **True filter action** ✅ |\n19: \n20: ### 1.2 `FunnelButton` consumers (all mobile navigation toggles)\n21: \n22: | # | File | Line | Usage | Kind |\n23: |---|------|------|-------|------|\n24: | 3 | `src/lib/components/feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte` | 31 | `<FunnelButton onclick={toggleMobile} top={3} />` — reveals the hidden feed list drawer on mobile (display block/none). | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n25: | 4 | `src/lib/components/contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte` | 34 | `<FunnelButton onclick={toggleMobile} />` — reveals the address-book navigation drawer on mobile. | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n26: | 5 | `src/lib/components/todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte` | 64 | `<FunnelButton onclick={() => (open = true)} top={6} />` — opens the full-screen mobile todo navigation drawer (workspaces, categories, priority, status, effort, due, tags). | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n27: | 6 | `src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte` | 141 | `<FunnelButton onclick={toggleMobile} />` — reveals the hidden time-tracking navigation drawer on mobile. | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n28: | 7 | `src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte` | 44 | `<FunnelButton onclick={() => (open = true)} />` — opens the full-screen mobile notes/categories navigation drawer. | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n29: \n30: ### 1.3 Hamburger precedent (correct pattern already in the codebase)\n31: \n32: - `src/lib/components/ui/buttons/HamburgerButton.svelte` — byte-for-byte identical to `FunnelButton` except it renders `IconMenu` (`@lucide/svelte/icons/menu`) instead of `IconFunnel`.\n33: - `src/lib/components/settings/SettingsNavigationMobile.svelte` (lines 4, 24) — the settings mobile drawer already uses `HamburgerButton`. This is the exact scenario the other mobile drawers are in, done right.\n34: \n35: ### 1.4 Dead code: unused `IconFunnel` imports\n36: \n37: These files import `IconFunnel` but never render it (leftover from an earlier version that rendered the icon directly):\n38: \n39: - `src/lib/components/feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte` — line 3\n40: - `src/lib/components/contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte` — line 11\n41: - `src/lib/components/todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte` — line 7\n42: - `src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte` — line 5\n43: \n44: ## 2. Where the funnel icon makes sense\n45: \n46: **Only `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte`.** The button's sole purpose is to open a filter panel that narrows the library list (genre, rating, wishlist, lent books, recipe type, plant location, unidentified). \"Funnel = filter\" is the canonical association in every major icon set. **Keep it as-is.**\n47: \n48: ## 3. Where the funnel icon does NOT make sense\n49: \n50: All six remaining usages (rows 1, 3–7 above) are mobile **navigation drawer / menu toggles**. The funnel icon semantically promises \"filter/sort the current content\", but the action actually opens a navigation menu (feeds list, address books, todo sections, time-tracking nav, note categories). A funnel on a menu button is misleading — it reads as \"filter\" to users who then land on a navigation drawer.\n51: \n52: Note on `TodoNavigationMobile.svelte` specifically: although the drawer *contains* filter sections (priority, status, due, tags, …), the button itself is a drawer opener — the same role `HamburgerButton` plays in settings. A funnel there still misleads, and switching only that one to a \"filter-like\" icon would make the mobile nav affordances inconsistent across modules.\n53: \n54: ## 4. Recommended replacements\n55: \n56: | Location | Current | Recommended | Rationale |\n57: |----------|---------|-------------|-----------|\n58: | `libraries/filters/Filter.svelte` | `funnel` | **keep `funnel`** | Genuine filter action; funnel is the canonical filter glyph. |\n59: | `feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte` | `FunnelButton` | **`HamburgerButton`** (`menu`) | Drawer toggle, not a filter. `top={3}` prop is supported by `HamburgerButton`. |\n60: | `contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte` | `FunnelButton` | **`HamburgerButton`** (`menu`) | Drawer toggle, not a filter. |\n61: | `todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte` | `FunnelButton` | **`HamburgerButton`** (`menu`) | Drawer opener; `top={6}` prop is supported. |\n62: | `time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte` | `FunnelButton` | **`HamburgerButton`** (`menu`) | Drawer toggle, not a filter. |\n63: | `notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte` | `FunnelButton` | **`HamburgerButton`** (`menu`) | Drawer opener, not a filter. |\n64: \n65: **Recommended replacement icon: `menu` (hamburger)** — via the existing `HamburgerButton` component, which is API-compatible with `FunnelButton` (`onclick`, `top`, `left` props) and already the convention for settings.\n66: \n67: **Alternatives considered and rejected:**\n68: - `list-filter` / `sliders-horizontal` — appropriate for an *inline filter control* (e.g. a filter toolbar in a list view header), not for a drawer opener. If the app ever adds a dedicated filter control on desktop, these are the better fits there. Both exist in the pinned version (see §5).\n69: - `align-justify` / `panel-left-open` — plausible menu glyphs, but `menu`/hamburger is the established convention in this app (settings) and the least surprising to users.\n70: \n71: ### Recommendation for `FunnelButton` itself\n72: \n73: Once the five consumers are switched to `HamburgerButton`, `FunnelButton` has no consumers left and becomes a pure duplicate of `HamburgerButton` (same markup, same props, different icon). Recommendation: **deprecate and delete `FunnelButton`**, and have consumers use `HamburgerButton`. (Do **not** just repoint `FunnelButton` to the hamburger icon — that would leave two identical components, which is worse than having one.) This is a follow-up implementation job; this assessment only documents the decision.\n74: \n75: ### Cleanup alongside the replacements\n76: \n77: - Remove the four unused `IconFunnel` imports: `FeedNavigation.svelte` (line 3), `ContactNavigation.svelte` (line 11), `TodoNavigationMobile.svelte` (line 7), `TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte` (line 5).\n78: \n79: ## 5. Icon availability in the pinned lucide version\n80: \n81: Pinned dependency: `@lucide/svelte` **0.544.0** (exact, in `package.json` devDependencies). `node_modules` is not installed in the worktree, so availability was verified against the published `@lucide/svelte@0.544.0` package file listing (jsDelivr data API).\n82: \n83: | Icon | Exists in 0.544.0 |\n84: |------|-------------------|\n85: | `funnel` (current) | ✅ |\n86: | `menu` (recommended replacement) | ✅ (already imported by `HamburgerButton.svelte`) |\n87: | `list-filter` (alternative) | ✅ |\n88: | `sliders-horizontal` (alternative) | ✅ |\n89: | `filter` / `filter-x` / `funnel-x` / `align-justify` / `sliders` (other candidates) | ✅ |\n90: \n91: No recommended icon is missing from the pinned version; no dependency change is required.\n92: \n93: ## 6. Conclusion\n94: \n95: - **Keep** the funnel on the library filter button (`Filter.svelte`).\n96: - **Replace** the funnel on all five mobile navigation toggles with the `menu`/hamburger icon via the existing `HamburgerButton`.\n97: - **Deprecate/delete** `FunnelButton` once it has no consumers.\n98: - **Remove** the four unused `IconFunnel` imports.\n99: - All replacements are available in the pinned `@lucide/svelte` 0.544.0 — no version bump needed.\n100: \n101: **Scope note:** per the job brief, this is an assessment only — no source files were changed.\n\n(End of file - total 101 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Assessment: funnel icon usage\n\nid: drama\nstatus: open\ndate: 2026-08-16\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `funnel` icon (`@lucide/svelte/icons/funnel`) is used in **7 places** across the codebase. Exactly **one** of them is a semantically correct use of a funnel — the library filter button in `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte`. The remaining **6** are all mobile navigation/drawer toggles, where the funnel icon is inappropriate: users reading a funnel expect \"filter this list\", but the button actually opens a navigation drawer/menu. This assessment recommends replacing every non-filter usage with a `menu` (hamburger) icon, which the codebase already ships as `HamburgerButton` (used by settings).\n\n## 1. Where the funnel icon is used (full audit)\n\n### 1.1 Direct `IconFunnel` renders (visible funnel icons)\n\n| # | File | Line(s) | Context | Kind |\n|---|------|---------|---------|------|\n| 1 | `src/lib/components/ui/buttons/FunnelButton.svelte` | 2, 15 | Floating circular button (`absolute`, `lg:hidden` = mobile-only), renders `<IconFunnel class=\"text-c-neutral-1\" />`. This is the icon *source* for every `FunnelButton` consumer. | Icon source for mobile toggles |\n| 2 | `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte` | 2, 60 | `<IconFunnel />` inside the libraries filter button; clicking opens the filter dropdown (genres, rating, wishlist, lent books, recipe/plant filters, clear filters). | **True filter action** ✅ |\n\n### 1.2 `FunnelButton` consumers (all mobile navigation toggles)","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md","text":"# Assessment: funnel icon usage\n\nid: drama\nstatus: open\ndate: 2026-08-16\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `funnel` icon (`@lucide/svelte/icons/funnel`) is used in **7 places** across the codebase. Exactly **one** of them is a semantically correct use of a funnel — the library filter button in `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte`. The remaining **6** are all mobile navigation/drawer toggles, where the funnel icon is inappropriate: users reading a funnel expect \"filter this list\", but the button actually opens a navigation drawer/menu. This assessment recommends replacing every non-filter usage with a `menu` (hamburger) icon, which the codebase already ships as `HamburgerButton` (used by settings).\n\n## 1. Where the funnel icon is used (full audit)\n\n### 1.1 Direct `IconFunnel` renders (visible funnel icons)\n\n| # | File | Line(s) | Context | Kind |\n|---|------|---------|---------|------|\n| 1 | `src/lib/components/ui/buttons/FunnelButton.svelte` | 2, 15 | Floating circular button (`absolute`, `lg:hidden` = mobile-only), renders `<IconFunnel class=\"text-c-neutral-1\" />`. This is the icon *source* for every `FunnelButton` consumer. | Icon source for mobile toggles |\n| 2 | `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte` | 2, 60 | `<IconFunnel />` inside the libraries filter button; clicking opens the filter dropdown (genres, rating, wishlist, lent books, recipe/plant filters, clear filters). | **True filter action** ✅ |\n\n### 1.2 `FunnelButton` consumers (all mobile navigation toggles)\n\n| # | File | Line | Usage | Kind |\n|---|------|------|-------|------|\n| 3 | `src/lib/components/feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte` | 31 | `<FunnelButton onclick={toggleMobile} top={3} />` — reveals the hidden feed list drawer on mobile (display block/none). | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n| 4 | `src/lib/components/contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte` | 34 | `<FunnelButton onclick={toggleMobile} />` — reveals the address-book navigation drawer on mobile. | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n| 5 | `src/lib/components/todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte` | 64 | `<FunnelButton onclick={() => (open = true)} top={6} />` — opens the full-screen mobile todo navigation drawer (workspaces, categories, priority, status, effort, due, tags). | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n| 6 | `src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte` | 141 | `<FunnelButton onclick={toggleMobile} />` — reveals the hidden time-tracking navigation drawer on mobile. | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n| 7 | `src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte` | 44 | `<FunnelButton onclick={() => (open = true)} />` — opens the full-screen mobile notes/categories navigation drawer. | Navigation/menu toggle ❌ |\n\n### 1.3 Hamburger precedent (correct pattern already in the codebase)\n\n- `src/lib/components/ui/buttons/HamburgerButton.svelte` — byte-for-byte identical to `FunnelButton` except it renders `IconMenu` (`@lucide/svelte/icons/menu`) instead of `IconFunnel`.\n- `src/lib/components/settings/SettingsNavigationMobile.svelte` (lines 4, 24) — the settings mobile drawer already uses `HamburgerButton`. This is the exact scenario the other mobile drawers are in, done right.\n\n### 1.4 Dead code: unused `IconFunnel` imports\n\nThese files import `IconFunnel` but never render it (leftover from an earlier version that rendered the icon directly):\n\n- `src/lib/components/feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte` — line 3\n- `src/lib/components/contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte` — line 11\n- `src/lib/components/todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte` — line 7\n- `src/lib/components/time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte` — line 5\n\n## 2. Where the funnel icon makes sense\n\n**Only `src/lib/components/libraries/filters/Filter.svelte`.** The button's sole purpose is to open a filter panel that narrows the library list (genre, rating, wishlist, lent books, recipe type, plant location, unidentified). \"Funnel = filter\" is the canonical association in every major icon set. **Keep it as-is.**\n\n## 3. Where the funnel icon does NOT make sense\n\nAll six remaining usages (rows 1, 3–7 above) are mobile **navigation drawer / menu toggles**. The funnel icon semantically promises \"filter/sort the current content\", but the action actually opens a navigation menu (feeds list, address books, todo sections, time-tracking nav, note categories). A funnel on a menu button is misleading — it reads as \"filter\" to users who then land on a navigation drawer.\n\nNote on `TodoNavigationMobile.svelte` specifically: although the drawer *contains* filter sections (priority, status, due, tags, …), the button itself is a drawer opener — the same role `HamburgerButton` plays in settings. A funnel there still misleads, and switching only that one to a \"filter-like\" icon would make the mobile nav affordances inconsistent across modules.\n\n## 4. Recommended replacements\n\n| Location | Current | Recommended | Rationale |\n|----------|---------|-------------|-----------|\n| `libraries/filters/Filter.svelte` | `funnel` | **keep `funnel`** | Genuine filter action; funnel is the canonical filter glyph. |\n| `feeds/FeedNavigation.svelte` | `FunnelButton` | **`HamburgerButton`** (`menu`) | Drawer toggle, not a filter. `top={3}` prop is supported by `HamburgerButton`. |\n| `contacts/ContactNavigation.svelte` | `FunnelButton` | **`HamburgerButton`** (`menu`) | Drawer toggle, not a filter. |\n| `todos/TodoNavigationMobile.svelte` | `FunnelButton` | **`HamburgerButton`** (`menu`) | Drawer opener; `top={6}` prop is supported. |\n| `time-tracking/TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte` | `FunnelButton` | **`HamburgerButton`** (`menu`) | Drawer toggle, not a filter. |\n| `notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte` | `FunnelButton` | **`HamburgerButton`** (`menu`) | Drawer opener, not a filter. |\n\n**Recommended replacement icon: `menu` (hamburger)** — via the existing `HamburgerButton` component, which is API-compatible with `FunnelButton` (`onclick`, `top`, `left` props) and already the convention for settings.\n\n**Alternatives considered and rejected:**\n- `list-filter` / `sliders-horizontal` — appropriate for an *inline filter control* (e.g. a filter toolbar in a list view header), not for a drawer opener. If the app ever adds a dedicated filter control on desktop, these are the better fits there. Both exist in the pinned version (see §5).\n- `align-justify` / `panel-left-open` — plausible menu glyphs, but `menu`/hamburger is the established convention in this app (settings) and the least surprising to users.\n\n### Recommendation for `FunnelButton` itself\n\nOnce the five consumers are switched to `HamburgerButton`, `FunnelButton` has no consumers left and becomes a pure duplicate of `HamburgerButton` (same markup, same props, different icon). Recommendation: **deprecate and delete `FunnelButton`**, and have consumers use `HamburgerButton`. (Do **not** just repoint `FunnelButton` to the hamburger icon — that would leave two identical components, which is worse than having one.) This is a follow-up implementation job; this assessment only documents the decision.\n\n### Cleanup alongside the replacements\n\n- Remove the four unused `IconFunnel` imports: `FeedNavigation.svelte` (line 3), `ContactNavigation.svelte` (line 11), `TodoNavigationMobile.svelte` (line 7), `TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte` (line 5).\n\n## 5. Icon availability in the pinned lucide version\n\nPinned dependency: `@lucide/svelte` **0.544.0** (exact, in `package.json` devDependencies). `node_modules` is not installed in the worktree, so availability was verified against the published `@lucide/svelte@0.544.0` package file listing (jsDelivr data API).\n\n| Icon | Exists in 0.544.0 |\n|------|-------------------|\n| `funnel` (current) | ✅ |\n| `menu` (recommended replacement) | ✅ (already imported by `HamburgerButton.svelte`) |\n| `list-filter` (alternative) | ✅ |\n| `sliders-horizontal` (alternative) | ✅ |\n| `filter` / `filter-x` / `funnel-x` / `align-justify` / `sliders` (other candidates) | ✅ |\n\nNo recommended icon is missing from the pinned version; no dependency change is required.\n\n## 6. Conclusion\n\n- **Keep** the funnel on the library filter button (`Filter.svelte`).\n- **Replace** the funnel on all five mobile navigation toggles with the `menu`/hamburger icon via the existing `HamburgerButton`.\n- **Deprecate/delete** `FunnelButton` once it has no consumers.\n- **Remove** the four unused `IconFunnel` imports.\n- All replacements are available in the pinned `@lucide/svelte` 0.544.0 — no version bump needed.\n\n**Scope note:** per the job brief, this is an assessment only — no source files were changed.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":101,"totalLines":101,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/archive/drama_funnel-icon-assessment/assessment.md","time":{"start":1791623359966,"end":1791623360067}},"id":"prt_12512ed94001Z0mK43Gx9F5p1r","sessionID":"ses_edaed43d5ffeRlWR2XlMWa9yDH","messageID":"msg_12512e940001KJv4GRf1xoGffo"}}
