{"type":"text","timestamp":1791623596419,"sessionID":"ses_edaec2704ffeWB9idQ36MdrQEO","part":{"id":"prt_1251680f000123ne2raCAd1Lpa","messageID":"msg_125167a3f001BeWJR3bBzSaQ2G","sessionID":"ses_edaec2704ffeWB9idQ36MdrQEO","type":"text","text":"Done. All six tasks are complete and committed on `chore/whom_assessment-time-tracking` (the branch named in `brief.md`).\n\n## What I did\n\nThis was an **assessment-only** job — no source files changed. The deliverable is `docs/jobs/whom_assessment-time-tracking/assessment.md`, following the `drama_funnel-icon-assessment` precedent of placing the report in the job directory.\n\n**TASK-1–5 (audits)** all folded into the report. Headline findings, every claim cited to `file:line`:\n\n- **Navigation/IA**: dashboard/entries view lives in store `activeTab` while both nav links share one href (`TimeTrackingNavigation.svelte:156-181`), so reload/deep-link/back can't restore the view; mobile drawer uses inline `style.display` instead of the app's `{#if open}` + transition pattern; project/category management is buried in the sidebar with hover-only and double-click affordances.\n- **Data model**: `project.total_duration` is dead while durations are recomputed in three places; `has_exact_times` can't be edited (absent from the update request); duration-only entries are anchored to the current wall-clock time and can roll into the previous day; project colour = first category colour; `uncategorized` fallback exists for a state the API forbids.\n- **CRUD**: `EntryCreate`/`EntryEdit` are ~90% duplicate and disagree on timestamps/timezones; silent validation no-ops; project delete is confirmed on the detail page but immediate in the sidebar; entries are editable from only one of three surfaces showing them.\n- **Timer/dashboard/statistics**: the real timer is honest; Pomodoro is a fourth unintegrated, non-persisted timer; the dashboard stacks the full statistics panel onto itself; `groupByProject` is duplicated verbatim.\n- **Visual/a11y/i18n**: raw hand-styled inputs beside shared controls, three different hard-coded colour fallbacks, contrast/labelling gaps, six unused i18n keys and an orphaned `dev.features.timeTracking` tip block (all four locales verified in sync).\n\nThe report ends with a prioritised 15-item follow-up table (impact/effort/files) so a future implementation job can pick items up.\n\n## Commits\n- `880f5c9` — assessment document (TASK-1..6)\n- `755d656` — implementation summary\n\nWorktree is clean. One flagged item in `implementation.md`: the report lives in the job directory per the `drama` precedent; if a top-level `docs/` path was intended, that's a one-line move.","time":{"start":1791623594224,"end":1791623596415}}}
